# KWETUU — Cursor Build Rules

## Identity
You are extending Kwetuu on the existing BusinessOS Vite + React + Supabase app.
Do not create a new project. Do not run create-react-app or create-next-app.

## First rule
Read SCHEMA_AUDIT.md and FEATURE_AUDIT.md.
Do not assume a `stores` table — tenants are `businesses` + `storefronts`.
Do not assume React Router v6 — routing is TanStack Router (file routes in `src/routes/`).

## Stack constraints
- Framework: Vite + React + TanStack Start only. No Next.js, Remix, or CRA.
- Database: Existing Supabase project only. No new projects. No Prisma/Drizzle.
- Auth: Existing Supabase Auth (`src/lib/auth/`). No Clerk, Auth0, or NextAuth.
- Payments: Paynow Zimbabwe (`paynow` npm) only. Shop keys in `store_paynow_credentials`. Platform billing keys are separate. No Stripe/PayPal.
- Paynow calls: server-side (`*.server.ts` / Cloud Run webhook `/api/webhooks/paynow`). Not the browser. Do not add duplicate Edge Functions unless asked.
- State: TanStack Query + existing cart helper. No Redux.
- Icons: lucide-react (already installed)
- UI: existing `src/components/ui/` shadcn copies
- Toasts: sonner (already installed)

## What NOT to do
- Never replace working code without being asked
- Never hardcode products, orders, or user data as if they were live shops
- Template gallery sketches must stay labelled as samples
- Never copy authentication from reference repos
- Never bypass RLS / never query another business’s rows from the client
- Never deduct shop stock on the client
- Never mark a Paynow order paid from the return URL alone — only the server webhook

## Multi-tenancy
Merchant-owned tables use `business_id` (not `store_id`).
Dashboard data goes through existing server functions and RPCs.
Public shop data goes through published-storefront RPCs.

## Reference repos (layout only)
- vercel/commerce, medusajs/nextjs-starter-medusa, storefront-ui — JSX/CSS patterns only
- cruip/mosaic-react, openstatusHQ/openstatus, shadcn data-table — dashboard patterns; we already have AppShell + DataTable
- paynowinc/paynow-node-sdk — already used on the server

## Stage order
1. Audit (SCHEMA_AUDIT.md + FEATURE_AUDIT.md) — done in git; keep them true
2. Public website (existing `/`, `/market`, `/pricing`, `/auth`; aliases `/stores`, `/signup`, `/login`)
3. Merchant dashboard (existing `/dashboard`, `/inventory`, `/storefront`)
4. Storefront templates (ten layouts, one catalogue — extend `store-experience.tsx`, do not add a second products API)
5. Checkout + Paynow (existing cart + checkout + webhook)
6. Path routing `/store/$slug` first; subdomains only when SHOP_HOSTS is on
7. Testing (tenant-isolation, stock, payment failure, mobile)

## File structure (actual)
src/routes/           TanStack file routes (not src/pages/)
src/components/ui/    shadcn
src/components/storefront/
src/lib/storefront/
src/lib/payments/     shop-paynow.server.ts, paynow.server.ts
src/lib/auth/
